CONCLUSION
  The most creative-looking ambient reframes are descriptive on this bank, not terminal: C3+Qsqrt(-7) still leaves 1 mixed kernel fiber.
  The first theorem-facing repair is the covering residue sheaf: mixed_kernel=0, mixed_route=0. The v2 word alone leaves mixed_kernel=1.
  The three-shadow packet (unit C3 slot, quadratic balance, and nonunit residue/v2 cover signature) also separates the bank, but it is intentionally more expensive.  Use it as the gluing interface; use the exact height word only as a debt detector for same-residue moves, not as a proof quotient.
  Assumption challenged: the tournament vertices need not be runners, arcs, or residues.  Here the useful vertices are proof sidecars and shadow-charge carriers.  Preserved predicate: theorem-exit separability for LRC14 packet rows.  Destroyed coordinate: exact height/endpoint owner/off-grid floor unless retained or routed to named debt.
